Looking at this problem, I need to find the exponent $k$ of $(1-x^{32})$ in $p(x) = (1-x)^a(1-x^2)^b(1-x^3)^c \cdots (1-x^{32})^k$, given that the coefficient of $x^1$ is $-2$ and coefficients of $x^2, \ldots, x^{32}$ are all zero.

